WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.820
Getting ten people into a game on Discord? Good luck. Everyone's typing… and nobody knows who's playing.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.090
With CreateYourQueue, everything is set up from the dashboard. Zero commands to type.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.560
A name for the queue, the format — two teams of five — and you're done.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.780
On the right, the preview shows the exact message the bot will post.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.270
Save… and open the queue!

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:33.530
The announcement drops in the channel. One click on the check mark, join the waiting room… and the queue fills itself.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.890
Ten out of ten! The bot builds the teams and creates two voice channels…

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.600
… then moves every player into theirs. Automatically. Nobody hunts for their channel.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:56.560
After the match, everything follows: leaderboard, MMR, ranks, seasons, clans. And the queue can even open by itself, on schedule.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:02.370
The same dashboard protects your server too: anti-raid, anti-link, auto-clean.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:08.606
CreateYourQueue. Your server, ready in a few clicks.

